#11501
"East Bank of a River"
"Thick stands of gnarled pine and small temperate trees crowd this small road
to the north and east.  A temporary yet very sturdy-looking wooden bridge,
wide enough for two teams of horse, crosses a raging river to the west.  The
road looks new, judging by fresh-looking roots and stumps which have been
dragged to each side of the road, yet it is already rutted as if it sees a
great deal of heavy traffic.  It continues to the south, where it runs through
a small copse and then turns around the base of a large square tower.
"
