#11503
"Rutted Road - Nearing a Hill"
"A raging river comes from the northeast here, running along the eastern
side of the road and finally under a rough wooden bridge to the south.  The
rutted road that comes in from the west is unpaved, yet this part of the road
seems to have had a lot of work done to it: large, flat stones and straw have
been pounded into the ground, preventing this part of the path from sliding
off into the river.  Dense, low woods line the opposite bank of the river,
while lighter, more open woods stand on this side of the river and line the
heavily-rutted dirt road as it continues west.
"
