#11504
"Gently Sloping Dirt Road"
"Light, low woods rich in scrub oak to the north and south crowd the edges of
the dirt road.  Wide enough for two teams of horse, the path is littered with
freshly-removed stumps and recently-cut roots, suggesting that it is
relatively new.  Despite this, it appears to have seen heavy use, as it has
been flattened in places where the wheels of carts and feet of beasts pass
repeatedly.  The road slopes gently upwards into a clearing in the woods to
the west, while to the east it slopes downward until it meets a river and
turns south.
"
