#11505
"Southern Edge of a Clearing - Bottom of the Hill"
"Fresh stumps stud the ground on each side of the road here, remnants of the
forest that until recently stood here.  A large, steeply-sloping hill rises to
the north, a rutted dirt road going straight up it.  The top of the rise has
been flattened, and the edge of a construction site, littered with large
granite blocks and temporary wooden structures can be seen atop it.  A deeply-
rutted dirt road slopes gently downwards to the east, where it eventually
meets a river.
"
