#11506
"South of the Foundation of a Grand Cathedral"
"The foundations of a great cathedral spread out to the north, dwarfing the
surrounding landscape.  The low beginnings of great walls, one titanic block
of stone stacked upon another, already show the basic rectangular shape of the
building.  A gap in the low walls to the north is home to a stone archway
surrounded by a wooden scaffold: it will one day be a majestic entryway.
Placed against the infant wall to the west is a long, wooden structure large
enough to house all the labor required in the construction effort.  A steep,
impassible ravine drops off suddenly to the east, while a dirt road heads down
the hill into a clearing in the forest to the south.
"
""
