#11508
"Inside a Wooden Longhouse"
"The growing cathedral wall to the north forms one side of this long wooden
structure, with multiple bunks placed against it.  Wooden posts with thin logs
supported between them form the other side of the room to the south, while
thatch supported by wooden beams provides a makeshift yet effective roof.  The
longhouse extends slightly farther west than the wall to the north, forming a
wide doorway through which one can follow the wall around the corner as it
turns northwards.
"
