thick outer wall of the cathedral, only a fraction of their eventual height,
yet still tall enough to easily block passage in those directions.  Foundation
stones make up most of the floor, but gaps between stones and the occasional
spot where stones have yet to be placed would make walking somewhat difficult.
"
