#11511
"Chapel of the Sun"
"Thick walls of rough granite blocks grow from the foundation to the north and
east, the tallest part of the building yet made.  Their tops are sheathed in
wood, where the last pieces of stone have yet to be put in place.  A large,
circular hole has been left in the wall to the east, looking over the edge of
a steep drop towards where the sun must peek over the horizon at dawn.  Pure,
beautiful alabaster tiles lie in neat stacks against the wall to the north,
where some have already been used to cover the rough granite.  At the base of
the wall to the east is a stack of delicate-looking, translucent sheets of
rose quartz.  An archway to the south leads through a nonexistent wall into a
side room off the main hallway, which lies past the columns to the west.
"
"[Kotoktok] bless acode at dawn, only in final version
"
