#11512
"Cathedral - Grand Hallway"
"Functionally yet artfully designed columns, made to support the tons of stone
that will be above them, rise to the east and west, as yet unfinished.  Behind
the row of columns to the west stands a rough yet well-made wooden scaffold,
surrounding the growing outer wall of the cathedral, which is still quite low.
Loose dirt makes up the floor in this section of the construction site,
awaiting giant blocks of foundation stone.  To the south lies the main
entrance to the young cathedral, a stone archway almost completely finished
rising far above the low walls.  To the east is a side chapel, while to the
north is what seems to be the center of the building.
"
