#11513
"Inside a Wooden Hut"
"Despite the fact that this is obviously a temporary structure built against
the heavy granite blocks that make up the western wall of the cathedral,
someone has made a very comfortable home inside this small wooden hut.  A
mahogany writing desk has been placed against the eastern wall, appearing to
serve the tenant as a dining table, storage closet, and workplace - clean
dishes, spare clothing, and reams of neatly stacked paper cover or hang from
every available surface.  A brazier burns quietly along the northern wall, a
smooth and freshly-swept piece of granite kept underneath to prevent coals
from falling out and starting a fire.  Considering all the furniture which
fills this hut, there is barely room to stand, much less move about easily.
"
