of wooden slats laid side by side.  Cliffs fall off to the east, west, and
north where the cathedral's plateau comes to an abrupt end.  Directly under
the ceiling is a simple but beautiful altar of polished grey marble.  South of
here lies an enormous construction effort: large cubes of stone and rising
columns are set into the rock-and-dirt ground of the plateau.
