#11516
"Beneath a Pavilion - Lull in the Construction"
"A watertight roof of oiled canvas is suspended overhead, stretched over a
wooden frame.  The fabric is dense enough to protect against the elements,
while allowing light to penetrate easily.  Blocks of rough granite set into a
solid foundation form a massive wall to the south, rising above the roof of
the pavilion.  Against the wall is a large pile of roughly-cut timber, the
destiny of which is not readily apparent.  There is no wall to the east,
although there may as well be; a steep drop off the edge of the hill on which
the cathedral stands awaits anyone who ventures in that direction.  A similar
cliff lies to the north.  Large, unfinished load-bearing columns line what
appears to be the central hall of the cathedral to the west.
"
