#11517
"Before a Smoldering Forge"
"This wide, open cottage is obviously used as the shop for the blacksmith of
this bustling construction site.  A tin hood serves as a chimney above a heavy
hearth of dark brick; a bellows near the hearth is used to stoke the coals
prior to working with metals.  Only the northern wall is made of brick, while
the other parts of the structure are recently-cut wood.  Various hammers, iron
bars, and tongs hang on hooks on the west wall.  A sliding wooden door to the
east is wide enough to allow a wagon to be backed in to be loaded or for a
horse to be shoed.  A narrow ladder leads upstairs into a small loft.
"
