#11519
"A Comfortable Loft"
"Thick with the smells of ash and red-hot metal, this comfortable loft
overlooks the smith's workshop below.  Broad, tar-soaked timbers hold up a
roof made with thin tiles of stone or baked clay, presumably used instead of
much cheaper straw to prevent fires from breaking out.  Towards the western
edge of the loft the roof is quite low; a man would have to crawl in order to
fit.  A pile of rumpled clothing and soot-stained rags has accumulated on this
side of the loft -- apparently the smith is not as fastidious about his living
quarters as he is about his shop.  A relatively newly-built ladder offers
escape from the loft back into the workshop proper.
"
